REPUBLICAN OBSERVATION MODELS (traditional 509 BCE, c.160 BCE, 44 BCE)
- Project-authored schematic city geometry, separated by period; the animated
  reveal is not a claim that every building was constructed in the observed year.
  Public-building dates, versions, uncertainty and model ownership transfers:
  research/rome02_formal_prepare_phasing.md and research/rome02_formal_prepare.md.
- Early enclosure: Cifani (2016), late-6th-century reconstruction hypothesis,
  approximately 365 ha. The extent is not a measured occupied area. Ordinary
  houses use qualified contemporary comparisons from San Giovenale V:1 (2013);
  Rome's household boundaries, density, heights and roofs remain schematic or
  explicitly estimated. No later atrium/impluvium type is backdated to 509 BCE.
  Basis: research/rome02_early_whole_plan.md,
  research/rome02_early_cifani_basis.md and research/rome02_early_house_sources.md.
- Middle-Republic Palatine/Curiae: Panella, Rescigno and Ferrandes,
  Architetture perdute (2021), including the road orientation and physical
  boundary contact on printed p.88. Cosa V's House of Diana is a named form
  comparison, not a transplanted Roman street grid or a dated Rome census.
  The reconstructed Servian circuit's location is approximate, at roughly
  150 m scale of uncertainty. Basis: research/rome02_mid_whole_plan.md and
  research/rome02_continuous_window_sources.md.
- Late-Republic buildings and Pompey/Curia: the dated source catalogue and
  qualified plan/elevation branches in research/rome02_republic_forms.md,
  research/rome02_republic_whole_evidence_decisions.md and FACTS S149-S153.
  The 44 BCE model precedes Caesar's assassination. Gardens, open fields and
  housing layout/density retain the declared schematic and estimate limits;
  later imperial forms are not treated as Republican measurements.
- The 29 BCE Curia Iulia and 28 BCE Apollo Palatine models are observed together
  in 28 BCE, not described as two buildings constructed in the same year.
  Archaeological plans, reconstruction drawings and photographs are research
  references only; none is reproduced as an on-screen third-party image.

